WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
On the south Wales coast, at Port Talbot,

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.690
stands a steelworks.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.110
Toyota builds cars at
Burnaston, in Derbyshire.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.790
Its UK plants employ about 3,000 people.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.670
And in 1970, farmland outside Cambridge
became the UK's first science park.

6
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.310
A coast, a county, a university city.

7
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.730
Why does each industry pick
such a different place?

8
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.410
Is it simply wherever land is cheapest?

9
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.970
In this mission, you'll weigh the
factors that pull a firm to a site:

10
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.030
land, labour, raw
materials, energy, markets,

11
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.630
transport and policy.

12
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.750
Then you'll compare primary, secondary,
tertiary and quaternary industries,

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.650
and see how their needs can shift.

14
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.630
Your mission: explain why different
industries choose such different sites.
